{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "ויולך", :translit "va'yolekh", :gloss "and He led/moved"} {:he "ד' במס'", :translit "dalet be-masa", :gloss "four in the Masorah"} {:he "ויולך ה' את הים", :translit "va'yolekh Hashem et ha-yam", :gloss "and the LORD moved the sea"} {:he "ויולך אותם שמרונה", :translit "va'yolekh otam shomronah", :gloss "and he led them to Samaria"} {:he "סנורים", :translit "sanverim", :gloss "blindness"} {:he "ויולך אותם אל מלך בבל", :translit "va'yolekh otam el melekh bavel", :gloss "and he led them to the king of Babylon"} {:he "ויולך חושך ולא אור", :translit "va'yolekh khoshekh ve-lo or", :gloss "and he walks in darkness and not light"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 4, :occurrences ["ויולך ה' את הים" "ויולך אותם שמרונה" "ויולך אותם אל מלך בבל" "ויולך חושך ולא אור"]}], :frame {:text "The Ba'al HaTurim first cites the four biblical occurrences of the phrase 'ויולך'. He connects the occurrence at II Kings 6:19 — where Elisha leads the smitten Arameans to Samaria — to our verse at Exodus 14:21, inferring that just as the Arameans were struck with סנורים, so too the Egyptians at the sea were struck with סנורים. The occurrence at Jeremiah 39:9 refers to Nebuzaradan leading exiles to the king of Babylon; the occurrence at Jeremiah 13:16, 'ויולך חושך ולא אור,' is read as a metaphor for the darkening of eyes in exile.", :sources ["II Kings 6:18-19" "Jeremiah 39:9" "Jeremiah 13:16" "Exodus 14:21"]}} {:quotes [{:he "ברוח קדים", :translit "be-ruach kadim", :gloss "with an east wind"} {:he "ב' במסו'", :translit "bet be-maso", :gloss "two in the Masorah"} {:he "ברוח קדים תשבר אניות תרשיש", :translit "be-ruach kadim tishbor oniyot tarshish", :gloss "with an east wind You shatter the ships of Tarshish"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["ברוח קדים" "ברוח קדים תשבר אניות תרשיש"]}], :frame {:text "The rare phrase 'ברוח קדים' appears at Exodus 14:21 describing the wind God used to split the sea, and at Psalm 48:8 where an east wind shatters ships of Tarshish. The Ba'al HaTurim links the two: the same east wind that split the sea also shattered all the ships that were in the sea at that moment.", :sources ["Exodus 14:21" "Psalm 48:8"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :masorah, :count 4, :occurrences ["ויולך ה' את הים" "ויולך אותם שמרונה" "ויולך אותם אל מלך בבל" "ויולך חושך ולא אור"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "ויולך ה' את הים", :refs [], :n 0, :lens :plene-insensitive} {:phrase "ויולך אותם שמרונה", :refs ["2 Kings 6:19"], :n 1, :lens :plene-insensitive} {:phrase "ויולך אותם אל מלך בבל", :refs ["Jeremiah 52:26"], :n 1, :lens :plene-insensitive} {:phrase "ויולך חושך ולא אור", :refs ["Lamentations 3:2"], :n 1, :lens :plene-insensitive}]} {:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["ברוח קדים" "ברוח קדים תשבר אניות תרשיש"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "ברוח קדים", :refs ["Exodus 14:21" "Psalms 48:8"], :n 2, :lens :exact} {:phrase "ברוח קדים תשבר אניות תרשיש", :refs ["Psalms 48:8"], :n 1, :lens :exact}]}], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:15:57.206369317Z", :model "glm-5.2"}